            Protein cereal is an expensive way to buy protein, but not equally expensive. Using the 2026 retail prices we found, Premier Protein Cereal works out to roughly $1.10 to $1.50 per 25 g of protein, depending on box size and whether you catch a Subscribe & Save price. Kashi GO is about $1.50 to $2.00, Catalina Crunch about $2.25, Three Wishes about $3.30 and Magic Spoon about $3.50 to $4.00. These figures move with every sale, so redo the math with the price on the listing.
          </p>

          <p>
            The formula is simple. Divide the price of the box by the number of servings, then divide by grams of protein per serving and multiply by 25. A 7 oz Magic Spoon box at about $10 with five 13 g servings, for example, gives about 65 g of protein, or roughly $3.85 per 25 g. A 9 oz Premier box at around $5 to $6 with about six 20 g servings gives about 120 g of protein, or close to $1.10 to $1.25 per 25 g.
